pkg:Evidence_v1_4_0 a quality:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Gate transcript for code-abundance-rdodi v1.4.0 (MINOR release)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "MINOR: re-verified this package's lineage against backlog-roadmap-framework's grown state (Lineage Operating Discipline v5.0.0 -> v7.0.0, TBox v1.54.0 -> v1.62.0, SHACL v1.65.0 -> v1.72.0, adding G19-G32). Re-read the full discipline fresh from GitHub bytes per B5/BP-D2, not from memory of the earlier version. Checked whether the LineageAdaptation construct (Assess/Fit-gap/Ruling/Re-link) applied: it does not -- its own Stage_Assess definition scopes it specifically to converting scope-last lineages to scope-first, and this lineage was already scope-first (independently re-verified by bidirectional traversal). Instead re-ran the actual mechanical checks against the grown vocabulary. Found and fixed: (1) a new Lineage/belongsToLineage requirement (v1.69.0 shape) that every WorkItem, and per the property's own definition every BacklogConcept, must declare -- added one Lineage individual and tagged all 27 applicable individuals in the register, not only the 5 that were mechanically flagged, per the framework's own G20 lesson about partial adoption; the new Lineage individual itself then needed lineageForMission/lineageOrdinal/lineageArchived, found and fixed in a second pass. (2) A genuine G31 violation in this session's own prior work: ObjRDODIDefaultGatesPassing's checkpoint used a fabricated calendar date (2026-09-15) for a metric whose real timing depends on unpredictable engineering work (Story 1 closing), not the calendar -- removed rather than kept as false precision, since it was not required at the declared L2 level; filed as a proposal (00-proposals/Proposal_BRSF_ConditionBasedCheckpoint_v1_0_0.md) since the shipped ObjectiveCheckpoint class has no condition-based form and minting one is not this session's vocabulary to extend (L-110/B1). Also checked G32 (exclusion rationale must cite the mission or a checked current fact, not legacy/unverified authority) against all 3 exclusions: clean, no fix needed. Both real checks re-verified after every fix: backlog_pipeline_verify_v1_0_0.py (order; 5/5 digests reproduce, unaffected throughout since the new content was outside the tracked stage types) and backlog_validate_v1_4_0.py at the declared L2_EvidenceBound level (0 sh:Violation, 86 sh:Warning -- legitimate advisories, not defects)."@en ;
    pub:transcriptSHA256 "d9136bbd8d2e8408c402dec46cc67b22819c258e99a6e869d47de1c73ebd0b4c"^^xsd:string .
